1. App overview
BFT QR Pay is a QR-code fare payment web application for Ben Franklin Transit (https://www.bft.org/), the public transit agency serving the Tri-Cities, WA (Kennewick, Pasco, Richland). It provides three core capabilities:

Scannable QR codes for payment — riders buy fares in-app and board by showing a tamper-proof QR code; operators scan it with a camera validator.
Data analytics tracking — every purchase, top-up, and boarding feeds an agency dashboard (KPIs, revenue/day, boardings by route, product mix, payment mix) plus a raw CSV export.
Proof of purchases — every transaction gets an immutable receipt number (BFT-YYYY-NNNNNN) and a printable receipt page.
Three surfaces:

Surface	URL	Users
Rider app	/	Riders: wallet, buy fare, show QR tickets, receipts
Fare validator	/static/scanner.html	Operators: camera scan, accept/reject, stop posters
Analytics dashboard	/static/dashboard.html	Agency staff: charts, KPIs, CSV export
Tech stack: Python 3.12 · FastAPI · SQLite (stdlib sqlite3) · qrcode[pil] for QR rendering · uvicorn server · vanilla JS frontend (no build step) · Chart.js 4.4.3 and html5-qrcode 2.3.8 from jsDelivr CDN.

2. Feature list
Demo auth: email-only sign-in, auto-creates account; session token in DB, cookie bft_session (httponly, samesite=lax, 30 days).
Wallet: simulated top-up ($1–$200, 4-digit card suffix); quick amounts $5/$10/$20/$50. Production: swap for Stripe/Adyen PaymentIntent.
Fare products (BFT 2025 fares):
Code	Name	Price	Reduced	Rides	Validity
SINGLE	Single Ride	$1.00	$0.50	1	2 h from first scan
DAY	Day Pass (mobile only)	$3.00	$1.50	unlimited	24 h
RIDE10	10-Ride Book	$8.00	$4.00	10	12 months
MONTH	Monthly Pass	$10.00	$5.00	unlimited	30 days
YEAR	Yearly Pass (mobile only)	$120.00	$60.00	unlimited	12 months
Reduced fare toggle (Youth / Senior / Disability pricing).
QR tickets: payload BFT1:<ticket_id>:<hmac-sha256[:16]> signed with a per-install secret (data/.secret, 64 hex chars, created once). All ticket state resolved server-side at scan time — payloads cannot be forged, edited, or replayed.
Fare validation: camera scan (html5-qrcode, rear camera) or manual payload entry → POST /api/validate → accept/reject banner + local log + server-side boarding record.
Stop posters: server-rendered PNG QR per stop; scanning deep-links the rider app with ?stop=CODE and shows a buy-fare banner.
Receipts: every top-up/purchase recorded; printable proof-of-purchase page with Print/Save-as-PDF.
Analytics: 7/30/90-day ranges, 6 KPI tiles, 4 Chart.js charts, recent transactions/validations tables, CSV export. Rider emails masked (j***@domain) and CSV uses R-<sha1[:8]> references.
Demo data: first run seeds 15 BFT routes, 8 stops, 5 fare products, and ~90 days of deterministic synthetic purchases/boardings (seed 42).
