4. Logical flow (user journeys)
Rider pays: sign in → wallet top-up (simulated card) → Buy Fare tab → pick product (+ optional reduced pricing) → POST /api/purchase debits wallet, mints ticket, records receipt → QR appears under My Tickets.

Rider boards: show QR → operator scans → POST /api/validate → server verifies HMAC → checks existence → status → expiry → rides → consumes ride / decrements / marks used → boarding logged → green ✅ ACCEPTED or red ❌ REJECTED banner on the validator.

Proof of purchase: Receipts tab lists transactions → "View" opens /static/receipt.html?id=BFT-YYYY-NNNNNN → printable receipt with ticket details.

Agency analytics: Dashboard → choose 7/30/90 days → KPIs + charts + recent activity → Export CSV.

5. Code workflow (request lifecycle)
POST /api/session — upsert account, create session row, set cookie.
POST /api/topup — validate amount + card suffix, credit wallet, write transaction with next receipt number.
POST /api/purchase — load product, price (reduced?), 402 if wallet short, insert ticket (tkt_<hex>, active, rides/expiry from product), debit wallet, write transaction, return QR data-URI + payload.
POST /api/validate — check_qr_payload (constant-time hmac.compare_digest) → load ticket → status → expiry → rides → consume (rides_remaining - 1, first_used_at via COALESCE, used at 0) → insert boarding row (accepted/rejected) → verdict JSON with masked rider ref (R- + SHA1(email)[:8]).
GET /api/admin/analytics?days=N — KPIs, revenue_by_day, rides_by_route, product_breakdown, revenue_by_method, recent_transactions (masked), recent_validations.
GET /api/admin/export.csv — full ledger as CSV, rider references hashed.
